      "writtenOn": "2025-11-14T20:03:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If I\u0027m understand this allocation function correctly, the goal is to return an innerPM of exactly size, with allocated padding. If that is correct then I think there is a bug here:\n\nBy passing the post-padding size to `SkIRect::MakePtSize({padding, padding}, size)))` you get a rect of `size + padding * 3`.\n\nThen, inside `extractSubset` you set srcRect with the `size + padding * 2`. This results in an intersection of `{0,0, size + padding * 2, size + padding * 2} with  {padding, padding, size + padding * 3, size + padding * 3}`\n\nThis results in an innerPM with size of `size + padding` instead of `size.`",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 34,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 34,
        "endChar": 99
      },
      "fixSuggestions": [
        {
          "fixId": "b9a3632f_1d56fd70",
          "description": "prompt_to_edit API",
          "replacements": [
            {
              "path": "src/gpu/graphite/RasterPathUtils.cpp",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 34,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 35,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "    SkAssertResult(outerPM.extractSubset(\u0026innerPM,\n                                         SkIRect::MakeXYWH(padding, padding,\n                                                           size.fWidth, size.fHeight)));\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "revId": "396cd13de5d1a5974b2f8590b94aea85ff8ce964",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
